{"id":"u-de78c924-5530-4a59-825a-a9fd0ff5d819","src":"community","title":"Greg's X-Frame System","author":"Greg H.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/AgdnYz-boostcampxframev31aiimport","desc":"The Philosophy\nThis isn't a generic Push/Pull/Legs split. The X-Frame Specialization Program is a highly targeted, 5-day aesthetic blueprint designed to build extreme structural width and lower-body sweep while keeping the waist tight. By prioritizing the exact muscle groups that create the classic \"X\" silhouette at the beginning of your workouts when your central nervous system is 100% fresh, this program turns lagging weak points into dominating stage-ready strengths.\n\nWho It's For\nThis is built for intermediate to advanced lifters focusing on body recomposition, Classic/Men's Physique aesthetics, or anyone looking to aggressively bring up lagging legs and shoulder width without over-training their chest or front delts.\n\nThe Core Strategy\n\nShoulder Specialization: Traditional overhead pressing is entirely eliminated to prevent front-delt takeover. Instead, the program hammers the side and rear delts with high-frequency isolation to build true 3D, capped shoulders that widen your frame.\n\nLat Width Over Thickness: Standard horizontal rows are swapped out for a strict battery of vertical pulling movements (weighted pull-ups, v-bar pulldowns, pullovers) to maximize the outer lat sweep.\n\nThe Outer Quad Sweep: Heavy barbell back squats are replaced by high-stability, quad-biased movements (Hack Squats, Heel-Elevated Smith Squats, Bulgarian Split Squats) to bypass lower-back fatigue and specifically target the vastus lateralis.\n\nStrategic Maintenance: The chest and arms receive precisely enough direct volume to stay full and dense without stealing systemic recovery from your primary X-Frame growth targets.\n\nThe Weekly Split\n\nDay 1: Quads & Delts (Heavy Bilateral)\n\nDay 2: Lats & Biceps\n\nDay 3: Chest & Hamstrings\n\nDay 4: Delts & Quads (Unilateral Focus)\n\nDay 5: Lats & Arms\n\nExecution Notes\nControl the eccentric (lowering) phase of every lift and leave your ego at the door. Maintain 1–2 Reps in Reserve (RIR) on your heavy compound movements to protect your central nervous system, and push the targeted isolation work on cables and machines to the brink of failure. Add sets as you progress.","level":["Novice","Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":90,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-08-01T20:58:27.126Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Quads & Delts","Lats & Biceps","Chest & Hamstrings","Delts & Quads","Lats & Arms"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Hack Squat","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":8,"x":3}],"note":"2 RIR; slow negative"},{"n":"Leg Extension","sets":[{"r":12,"x":3}],"note":"Pause at top"},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"x":4}],"note":"Drop set on last set"},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"x":4}],"note":"Constant tension"},{"n":"Standing Calf Raise","sets":[{"r":12,"x":3}],"note":"Deep stretch at bottom"}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Pull-Up (Weighted)","sets":[{"r":6,"x":3}],"note":"Depress scapula first"},{"n":"Lat Pulldown (Neutral Grip)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}],"note":"Hard stretch at top"},{"n":"Lat Pulldown (Single Arm)","sets":[{"r":12,"x":3}],"note":"Focus on lat sweep"},{"n":"Incline Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":12,"x":3}],"note":"Full stretch"},{"n":"Bayesian Curl","sets":[{"r":12,"rpe":9,"x":3}],"note":"1 RIR"}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":9,"x":3}],"note":"1-2 RIR"},{"n":"Chest Press (Machine)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}],"note":"Pause at bottom"},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}],"note":"Constant tension"},{"n":"Seated Hamstring Curl","sets":[{"r":12,"x":3}],"note":"Slow eccentric"},{"n":"Hanging Leg Raise","sets":[{"r":12,"x":3}],"note":"Control swing"}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Single Arm Cross Body Y-Raise","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"x":4}